---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout active="home" menu="Docs menu · Overview">
  <div class="body" style="max-width: 920px">
    <p class="eyebrow">Overview</p>
    <h1>Mru documentation</h1>
    <p class="lede" style="max-width: 40ch">
      Reference for Mru&#39;s open core: the shrinking-quorum runtime, the Dusk simulator, and the tools around them.
    </p>
    <div class="callout" style="margin: 24px 0 8px">
      <span class="tiny">Status</span>
      <span>
        Early. The runtime is a prototype at TRL 3, and its API will change. All code here is open source under Apache
        2.0. Mru 2049&#39;s bundled data keeps its own licences.
      </span>
    </div>

    <h2>Where to start</h2>
    <div class="cards two" style="margin-top: 8px">
      <a class="card" href="/concepts/shrinking-quorum/" style="text-decoration: none">
        <p class="k">Concepts</p>
        <h3 class="h3">Degradation-first design</h3>
        <p class="small soft" style="margin: 10px 0 0">
          The Degradation-First Principle, the shrinking quorum, and how we score a system that is always losing parts.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href="/core/quorum-crate/" style="text-decoration: none">
        <p class="k">Core runtime</p>
        <h3 class="h3">
          The <code>quorum</code> crate
        </h3>
        <p class="small soft" style="margin: 10px 0 0">
          Vote on three, compare on two, self-check on one. <code>no_std</code>, no allocation, checked with Kani.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href="/simulation/dusk/" style="text-decoration: none">
        <p class="k">Simulation</p>
        <h3 class="h3">Dusk</h3>
        <p class="small soft" style="margin: 10px 0 0">
          A Monte Carlo of redundancy policies on hardware that only ever decays. 10,000 missions in about two seconds.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href="/core/quorum-cli/" style="text-decoration: none">
        <p class="k">Integrations</p>
        <h3 class="h3">F&#180; and OPS-SAT</h3>
        <p class="small soft" style="margin: 10px 0 0">
          The plan for F&#180; components around the Rust core, and the operations note for running on OPS-SAT.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href="/lab/2049/" style="text-decoration: none">
        <p class="k">Lab</p>
        <h3 class="h3">Mru 2049</h3>
        <p class="small soft" style="margin: 10px 0 0">
          A browser flight simulator on real astronomical data. 109,389 stars, planets correct for any date.
        </p>
      </a>
    </div>

    <h2 id="quickstart">Quickstart</h2>
    <p>
      You need a Rust toolchain. Clone the runtime, run its tests, then run the demo with a stuck replica and a dead
      one.
    </p>
    <pre class="pre" tabindex="0"><span class="c"># the runtime and its demo</span>
git clone https://github.com/mruspace/flight
<span class="k">cd</span> flight
cargo test --workspace
cargo run --release -- --policy shrink --ticks 20000 --seed 1 \
  --upset-rate 0.001 --fault stuck:1@4000 --fault kill:0@9000</pre>
    <p style="margin-top: 16px">
      Run the same seed with <code>--policy tmr</code> to compare:
    </p>
    <pre class="pre" tabindex="0">quorum --policy tmr    ...  useful=8993  detected=11007 wrong=0 halted_at=never
quorum --policy shrink ...  <span class="s">useful=14490</span> detected=10    wrong=0 halted_at=never</pre>
    <p style="margin-top: 16px">Then the simulator, which needs no dependencies:</p>
    <pre class="pre" tabindex="0">git clone https://github.com/mruspace/dusk
<span class="k">cd</span> dusk
cargo run --release              <span class="c"># 10,000 missions, about 2 s</span>
cargo run --release -- --sweep   <span class="c"># sensitivity, about 30 s</span></pre>

    <h2>Where the code lives</h2>
    <div class="tbl-box" tabindex="0">
      <table class="tbl">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Repository</th>
            <th>What it is</th>
            <th>Language</th>
            <th>Status</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">
              <a href="https://github.com/mruspace/flight">mruspace/flight</a>
            </td>
            <td>Decision core and demo program</td>
            <td>Rust</td>
            <td class="m">v0.1.1 · TRL 3</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">
              <a href="https://github.com/mruspace/dusk">mruspace/dusk</a>
            </td>
            <td>Redundancy Monte Carlo</td>
            <td>Rust</td>
            <td class="m">0.1.0 · TRL 3–4</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">
              <a href="https://github.com/mruspace/2049">mruspace/2049</a>
            </td>
            <td>Browser flight simulator</td>
            <td>TypeScript</td>
            <td class="m">Lab</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="tiny" style="margin-top: 32px">
      Code Apache 2.0 · Whitepaper CC BY 4.0, doi:10.5281/zenodo.20579438 · Questions:{' '}
      <a href="https://mru.space/contact/">Request information</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
